def is_prime(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return False
    if n <= 3:
        return True
    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:
        return False
    i = 5
    while i * i <= n:
        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:
            return False
        i += 6
    return True
```
This function checks if a number is prime by first handling the easy cases (numbers less than 2, even numbers, and multiples of 3), then checking for factors from 5 upwards, only up to the square root of `n`, and skipping even numbers and multiples of 3.

